{"record": "turn", "turn": 4, "seconds": 6.91, "response_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_details": null, "blocks": ["thinking", "tool_use"], "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 2323}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2323, "cache_read_input_tokens": 8945, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 1077, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "tools": [{"id": "toolu_01C8g3YfpGvMyQXhFmYxQaNP", "name": "submit_answer", "arguments": {"answer": "No. The two analyses use different thresholds. The dSph gamma-ray limit is the one-sided 95% upper limit where 2[ln L_max − ln L(⟨σv⟩95)] = 2.71 (ΔTS = 2.71, or Δln L = 1.355). The AMS-02 antiproton limit is the upper endpoint of the ΔQ ≤ 3.84 region (Q = −2 ln L), the nominal one-parameter 95% interval threshold. The paper says this differs from the usual one-sided 2.71 prescription. The nuisance parameters also differ. The dSph analysis profiles over each dwarf's J-factor normalization (J = sJ0, Gaussian prior in log10 s, profiled over log10 s in [−3,3]). The antiproton analysis profiles over the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L (Gaussian penalty in log10 L with L̂ = 4.96 kpc and σ = 0.197, profiled over 1–12 kpc).", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}]}, "status": "answer", "error_kind": null, "seconds": 0.0}]}
{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261120T080453Z_dev-02_staged_e1d1", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "No. The two analyses use different thresholds. The dSph gamma-ray limit is the one-sided 95% upper limit where 2[ln L_max − ln L(⟨σv⟩95)] = 2.71 (ΔTS = 2.71, or Δln L = 1.355). The AMS-02 antiproton limit is the upper endpoint of the ΔQ ≤ 3.84 region (Q = −2 ln L), the nominal one-parameter 95% interval threshold. The paper says this differs from the usual one-sided 2.71 prescription. The nuisance parameters also differ. The dSph analysis profiles over each dwarf's J-factor normalization (J = sJ0, Gaussian prior in log10 s, profiled over log10 s in [−3,3]). The antiproton analysis profiles over the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L (Gaussian penalty in log10 L with L̂ = 4.96 kpc and σ = 0.197, profiled over 1–12 kpc).", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}]}, "turns": 4, "seconds": 11.833, "tool_calls": 4, "tool_result_chars": 19594, "input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 1397, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2323, "cache_read_input_tokens": 24305, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-20T08:05:05+00:00"}
